{
  "answer": "The record for the most consecutive female wheelchair singles titles, as recognized by Guinness World Records, is 15 titles, achieved by Diede de Groot at The Wimbledon Championships in **London, UK** on July 13, 2024 (Source: `https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/755535-most-consecutive-wheelchair-singles-titles-female` - E1).\n\nThe current Mayor of London, as of April 2025, is Sadiq Khan (Source: `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayor_of_London` - E4, E7, E8, E9).\n\nThe current spouse of Mayor Sadiq Khan is **Saadiya Khan** (or Saadiya Ahmed) (Source: `https://www.thesun.co.uk/news/14859504/who-is-sadiq-khans-wife-saadiya-khan/` - E3).",
